  "raw_label": "postponed_or_procedural",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Azhar Hussain vs The State Of Assam on 28 March, 2024 Page No.# 1/4 Gahc010048852024 The Gauhati High Court (High Court Of Assam, Nagaland, Mizoram And Arunachal Pradesh) Case No. : Crl.Rev.P./97/2024 Azhar Hussain S/O Abdul Jalil Vill- Lamajuar, P.S. Badarpur Dist. Karimganj, Assam Versus The State Of Assam Rep. By The Pp, Assam Advocate for the Petitioner : MR H R CHOUDHURY Advocate for the Respondent : PP, ASSAM BEFORE HON'BLE MR. JUSTICE KAUSHIK GOSWAMI 28.03.2024",
    "facts": "By way of this petition filed under Section 401 read with 482 Cr.P.C, the petitioner has sought setting aside and quashing of the impugned order dated 06.02.2024 passed by the learned Addl. Chief Judicial Magistrate, Karimganj in Badarpur P.S. Case No. 347/2023 rejecting the zimma prayer of the betel nuts of the petitioner. 3. Mr. B. Sarma, learned Addl. P.P. submits that the report dated 26.03.2024 received from the Investigating Officer indicates that the expert report of District Agricultural Office and the FSL report has been received. 4. It appears that as per the aforesaid FSL report, the sample of the seized betel nuts is opined to confirm to the prescribed standards as per Food Safety Regulations with respect to the tests carried Azhar Hussain vs The State Of Assam on 28 March, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/83183375/ 1 out. Further, in terms of the agricultural report of the expert, it appears that the betel nuts are not local in nature.",
    "arguments": ""
  },
